-- title:
--   Every finite adelic element has an integer multiple in widehatΛ
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$, i.e. $\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Lambda) = \top$ as a $\mathbb{Q}$-submodule of $D$. Write $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ for the finite adele ring `FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ` of $\mathbb{Q}$ relative to its ring of integers, and let [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) denote the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by those elements of the form $z \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a \in \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ such that $a_v$ lies in the valuation ring $v.\mathrm{adicCompletionIntegers}\ \mathbb{Q}$ of the completion at $v$ for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is: for every $w \in D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ there is a natural number $N \neq 0$ such that the scalar multiple $(N : \mathbb{Q}) \cdot w$ belongs to [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14). No finite generation of $\Lambda$, no multiplicative closure and no condition $1 \in \Lambda$ is assumed.
--
--   This is the fullness statement that the adelic box $\widehat\Lambda$ of a $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice satisfies $\mathbb{Q}\cdot\widehat\Lambda = D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, so that every finite adelic element of $D$ becomes integral after clearing a single denominator. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where adelic conjugation of lattices and the associated ideal sets are compared.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_exists_ne_zero_natCast_smul_mem_finiteAdeleBox.lean

